back to alternate cached policy if primary policy validation fails"}],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Ross","email":"jonross@chromium.org","date":"2026-10-01 21:48:01.000000000","tz":-420},"committer":{"name":"Chromium LUCI CQ","email":"chromium-scoped@luci-project-accounts.iam.gserviceaccount.com","date":"2026-10-01 21:48:01.000000000","tz":-420},"subject":"Restore non-volatile x64 registers in SuspendableThreadDelegateWin","message":"Restore non-volatile x64 registers in SuspendableThreadDelegateWin\n\nhttps://crrev.com/c/7708137 refactored GetRegistersToRewrite() into\nGetRegisters() and SetRegisters(). On Windows x64, 6 of the 9\nnon-volatile registers (R12, R13, R14, R15, Rdi, Rsi) were accidentally\ndropped, leaving only Rbx, Rbp, and Rsp.\n\nWhen a function uses one of the dropped non-volatile registers as its\nUNWIND_INFO FrameRegister (or stores a stack pointer in it), neither\nStackCopierSuspend::CopyStack nor StackCopier::CloneStack rewrote the\nregister to point into the copied/cloned StackBuffer. Consequently,\nRtlVirtualUnwind on the background sampling worker thread could\ndereference a stack address in the resumed target thread\u0027s live stack\n(after the frame had unwound or been unmapped) or in an uncloned buffer,\ncausing sporadic STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION (0xc0000005) crashes during\nStackSampler::WalkStack.\n\nRestore all 9 non-volatile registers on Windows x64 and add a unit test\nverifying GetRegisters() and SetRegisters() round-trip all expected\nnon-volatile registers.\n\nBug: 473587142, 402749159, 454752444\nChange-Id: I101a9941e2efb919b2324c7ae6580efcd2247dbe\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8482885\nCommit-Queue: Jonathan Ross \u003cjonross@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Sean Maher \u003cspvm@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1709431}\n"},"branch":"refs/heads/main","files":{"base/profiler/win32_stack_frame_unwinder_unittest.cc":{"old_mode":33188,"new_mode":33188,"old_sha":"c617f97d9343da8ae4f666e2a7da9d98de15e6ac","new_sha":"f90e99f8d836d78cb4074638d880b26d5e386050","lines_inserted":71,"size_delta":2115,"size":9379},"base/profiler/suspendable_thread_delegate_win.cc":{"old_mode":33188,"new_mode":33188,"old_sha":"6fe7880bb7cbffae92b3d54304cdf5f29a42ec1a","new_sha":"d934fda98048168b51c731ad0245919bcbb7127e","lines_inserted":17,"lines_deleted":4,"size_delta":474,"size":7484}},"description":"Rebase","conflicts":{"base":"8667e370cd8fa18aa6df82a2d4edd2e439fb66d4","ours":"4b76bc3d9d0a9893c2ed0460ac9176f7e58682a0","theirs":"1d1838464f15630596dc92e6c989e1bd4f83ae92","merge_strategy":"recursive","contains_conflicts":false}}}}
